From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:34:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] taskschd: keep all that a task definition says, and write and
 read it as Windows does.

A definition kept little more than a time or daily trigger, an executable
and a few settings, and wrote what it kept in its own format: Office's
tasks were stored with empty triggers, an empty principal and an Exec
action without a command.

Triggers of every kind now keep what their interfaces set, repetition
and schedules included, in a collection that removes by index or id.
Settings keep their idle and network settings, restart on failure and
what ITaskSettings2 adds; a principal keeps accounts as SIDs and gives
their names back, with the logon type they imply; the actions keep
their ids and context.

The XML is Windows': a UTF-16 declaration, CRLF line ends, the elements
in its order, and only what it writes when a value was set.  Reading
checks values the way Windows does and fails with the same SCHED_E_
errors, and ITaskNamedValueCollection::Item takes an index, as in the
SDK.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 56fadec73bd2591d6401c0c311ddddeb4e144808)

